# FinWatch application Kconfig

menu "FinWatch"

config FINWATCH_EXPANSION_MOCK
	bool "Use a mock expansion module instead of real I2C"
	default n
	help
	  Replaces the I2C transport for the modular expansion port with an
	  in-memory mock that serves a canned "Test Dial" descriptor and a
	  rotating input report.

	  This lets the enumeration state machine, descriptor validation and
	  module UI be developed and tested before any physical expansion
	  hardware exists. It also exposes fault-injection hooks so the
	  host's descriptor-rejection paths can actually be exercised.

	  Turn this off to talk to a real module over i2c3.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
